      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk i get why you'd say that but i feel like you're missing the point. mainstream science doesn't always catch everything right away. i'm not looking for a medical diagnosis, i'm looking for the logic behind how a human system could potentially align with a digital one. if we look at it from a systems theory perspective, isn't it possible that a person's physiological state could act as a kind of organic oscillator that's responding to the same data streams the algorithms are? like, if i wanted to actually test this, what kind of data should i be tracking alongside my trades to see if there's a real correlation?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
